Kian OS is a Linux-based desktop operating system on an Ubuntu LTS base.

  * Real apt:       sudo apt update && sudo apt full-upgrade
                    sudo apt install <pkg>
  * Real Bash:      every GNU coreutils command works
  * Install:        use the Welcome window that opens on the desktop, or
                    sudo kian-install   (asks mirror region + timezone,
                                        works fully offline like Ubiquity)
                    or the graphical installer (Calamares)
  * Persist:        sudo kian-persist   (save your live session FOR REAL:
                    files, /etc, apt installs survive reboot)
  * Login:          user `kian`, password `live` (live session default)
  * Sudo:           kian is in the sudo group; password is the user password
  * Root login is disabled; privilege escalation is via sudo only.

Thanks for trying Kian OS — https://github.com/kiantaei/Kian-OS
